    <div class="article-body">

        <p>Buying from U.S.-based sellers on Lively? Here's what you need to know about how shipping works, how much it might cost, and how long it usually takes.</p>

        <p><strong>On this page:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#how-it-works">How U.S. shipping works</a></li>
            <li><a href="#costs">Typical USPS shipping services costs</a></li>
            <li><a href="#delivery-times">Delivery times</a></li>
            <li><a href="#related">Related resources</a></li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="how-it-works">How U.S. shipping works</h2>

        <p>When you buy from a U.S. seller, your order ships through USPS, whether the destination is domestic or international. You won't need to choose a USPS shipping service because Lively does that for you.</p>

        <p>We automatically pick the most cost-effective USPS option based on:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>The product type/category</li>
            <li>The total weight and size of your shipment</li>
            <li>How far it's traveling between the seller and your address (measured by USPS Zones)</li>
            <li>The seller's shipping preferences and discounts</li>
        </ul>

        <p>You'll usually pay for shipping, unless the seller's offering a discount or free shipping.</p>
        <p>You'll see the total shipping cost for your item before checkout, and in your order receipt later.</p>

        <h2 id="costs">Typical USPS shipping services costs</h2>

        <p>Most orders ship using Lively's discounted prices or standard <a href="#">USPS commercial rates</a>:</p>

